# Example ReRDMFT input file: carbon monoxide (R = 1.128 Angstrom), 6-31G basis (co-6-31g.gbs, from
# https://www.basissetexchange.org/), GNOF (3 coupling subspaces of 2 orbitals), 4-component with the MIN-MAX stage
# (FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG), ADAM min-max and CHOLESKY TRUE. RKB basis of 72 spinors (36 negative-energy, 36 positive-energy).
# The first stage is the no-pair minimization over the positive-energy spinors (-112.9253454 Ha). FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG
# TRUE then continues from that minimum with rotations that also mix the 20 occupied positive-energy spinors
# (occupation > 1e-6) with the 36 negative-energy ones: ADAM descent-ascent converges the orbitals to the saddle point of order 720
# (energy maximized along those electron-positron directions, minimized along the rest), alternating with the full
# re-minimization of the occupation numbers. Measured: ~75 s in total, the min-max stage takes 2 macro-iterations and
# moves the energy by 1e-9 Ha. The check of the saddle type (dense diagonalization of the Hessian and count of its
# negative eigenvalues: 720 expected) runs only with DEBUG TRUE and adds ~2 minutes at this size.
# Measured: ~95 s in total; the min-max stage takes 4 ADAM macro-iterations and moves the energy by 1.3e-9 Ha (final -112.9253453815 Ha).
# Follow the run with `tail -f co_631g_c4_gnof_neg_adam_cholesky.live`.
NELEC 14
BASIS co-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
SCF_DIRECT_4C FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing SCF path (SCF_DIRECT_4C now defaults TRUE for plain C4_SPINOR runs)
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 3
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION_4C_NEG TRUE
MINMAX_ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER ADAM
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO
CHOLESKY TRUE
ON_DEMAND_ERI FALSE  # off here to keep this example's historical fast runtime (the whole packed AO tensor already fits in memory); default is TRUE, see lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization_cholesky.inp for the on-demand path demonstrated explicitly.

GEOMETRY
C   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.128000
END
